+`--kvmem-source-mib N` separately opts into process-local RAM source recording.
+It requires KVMem, one running request, one GPU, RAM and none/MTP execution;
+the current qualification uses ordinary decode and MTP4. Text is supported;
+media, grafts and custom position rows cannot be recorded by this adapter.
+The default is off while recovery integration is incomplete. This records
+source data and does not enable checkpoint persistence or KV reconstruction.
+
+The complete admitted prepared input is saved before the first prefill unit.
+Its accepted source frontier is distinct from the computed KV frontier, so a
+cancelled prefill can retain input it has not executed. Generated rows enter
+the source only after the complete Program commit succeeds; discarded MTP
+drafts and provisional output do not enter it. Source configuration binds the
+actual tokenizer, active template/arguments, model artifact and runtime schema.
+The digest is not permission to restore retired KV.
+
+S bounds the fixed 256-entry directory and actual token/event capacities,
+including old+new growth reservations. Store/account and bounded allocation
+control objects, allocator overhead and prepared-request workspace are outside
+S; it is not a process RSS or checkpoint bound. Full source directories or
+insufficient S reject capture/append without automatically forgetting records.
+Branches/expiry, system-wide forget, durable recovery and source-driven rebuild
+are not exposed by this recording option yet. A separate record is currently
+retained for each admitted request, including source accepted before a later
+execution failure.
+
+`/props` reports source quota/current/peak/denials, record count and last accepted/
+computed frontiers. `source_last_tokens_fnv1a64` is a diagnostic FNV-1a digest of
+little-endian int32 source rows, not an identity or integrity authority.
+`--kvmem-verify-transfers` also compares each new journal row directly with the
+accepted Program rows. Source allocation failures use the same request-local
+Unavailable cleanup as other explicit KVMem quota failures.
+
 `/props` reports `kvmem.gc_policy`, configured `gc_aux_budget_bytes`, and usage
 fields `gc_aux_budget_bytes`, `gc_aux_bytes`, `gc_aux_peak_bytes`, `gc_aux_denied`.
